.TH SCSI 4 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
scsi \- SCSI subsystem interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/scsi.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B scsi
driver provides a unified interface for accessing SCSI devices, including disks, optical drives, and generic passthrough devices.

.SS Device Nodes
The SCSI subsystem exposes the following device nodes under
.BR /dev/storage/ :
.TP
.B /dev/storage/scsi/B:T:L
Direct generic access to a specific SCSI device addressed by Bus (\fIB\fP), Target (\fIT\fP), and LUN (\fIL\fP). This interface accepts generic SCSI CDBs via ioctl.
.TP
.B /dev/storage/scsi/B
The bus controller node for bus \fIB\fP. This node accepts ioctls for bus management, such as device enumeration and rescanning.
.TP
.B /dev/storage/scsiN
Legacy-style or high-level block device alias (e.g., \fIscsi0\fP) mapping to the \fIN\fP-th detected block device (disk or CD-ROM). This serves as the primary interface for filesystems.

.SH IOCTLS
.TP
.B SCSI_IOCTL_SEND_COMMAND
Send a raw CDB to the device.
.TP
.B SCSI_IOCTL_GET_ID
Retrieve the Bus:Target:LUN triplet for the file descriptor.
.TP
.B SCSI_IOCTL_RESCAN_BUS
(Bus controller only) Trigger a scan of the SCSI bus for new devices.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sd (4),
.BR sr (4)
